==Old English==

===Etymology===
From ''[[ge-|ġe-]]'' + ''[[-rof#Old English|-rōf]]'' "number of, array of" from {{etyl|ang|-}} *{{term||rof|an array, number, host}} (attested only in compounds: [[secgrof|secgrōf]] ‘host of men’, [[stæfrof|stæfrōf]] ‘alphabet’). Cognate to modern Swedish [[greve]] ([[count]]).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/jeˈreːva/|lang=ang}}

===Noun===
{{ang-noun|g=m}}

# a [[reeve]] or official with local jurisdiction under the king; the chief magistrate of a district

